DSH WorkBuddy Harness — notes on provenance
===========================================

Fork origin
-----------
This repository started as a fork of `dsh-workbuddy`
(https://github.com/Faide-cyber/dsh-workbuddy), revision 9951d25 (v1.0.12),
released under the MIT License (Copyright (c) 2026 Faide-cyber).

Modifications in this repository (Copyright (c) 2026 bushizhanghan) are
MIT-licensed on the same terms. `LICENSE` carries both copyright lines, and the
reproducible diffs against upstream 1.0.12 live in `patches/`.

Changes relative to upstream 1.0.12:

1. Widened the `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` peer dependency ranges from the exact pin
   `0.2.0-rc.2` to `>=0.2.0-rc.2 <0.2.1 || >=0.2.1-0 <0.3.0-0`, so DeepSeek
   Harness 0.2.1 no longer rejects the plugin at load time.
2. Rewrote the client-name string `DeepSeek Harness` to `DeepSeek-Harness` in the
   outgoing chat request body, which the upstream service accepts as a known
   client name.
3. Renamed the package to `@bushizhanghan/dsh-workmate` and the repository to
   `bushizhanghan/dsh-workbuddy-harness`, including the client module id, the
   `cordis.patch.yml` insert name, the CLI command name and the documentation.
   The model provider id (`workbuddy-ai`) is unchanged.
4. Reorganised modules, naming, comments, build and CI wiring without changing
   behaviour; the README was rewritten without screenshots.

Third-party portions
--------------------
The host architecture (loopback shim, credential store, pi-ai adapter, probe
protocol) is adapted from `dsh-workbuddy-connect` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026
Corrine Hu). The full text of that license is kept in `LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY`.

If upstream ships an equivalent fix, prefer the official package.
